## Context
DESIGN.md §4 PR-7, honoring R14 and D1. Upstream logs a no-text attachment
once and re-encounters it forever (fulltext-source.ts) — no terminal state, so
coverage can never honestly reach 100% on a library with scanned PDFs. The PR:
the warn-once becomes a stored reason; the item counts covered as
metadata-only; metadata-only counts enter status per D1 (denominator = items,
metadata-only included, with reason). Terminal `empty` is done, not failed —
different bookkeeping, different sentence.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] no-text is a recorded terminal state, never retried until content changes
- [ ] status reports metadata-only counts per D1
- [ ] PR opened upstream; outcome recorded here

## Amendments (implementation review, 2026-08-26)
Feasible independently of 0018 at item granularity (a small
fulltext_state(item_key, reason) table / snapshot map), but both tickets
rewrite the same forty lines of fulltext-source.ts (the warn-once is
failures++ === 0 at :132) — hence Blocked-by 0018, sequenced not concurrent.
